  "notes": "West leads the ♥5 against 6♠. East wins the opening heart lead and continues the suit. South has a loser in both diamonds and clubs. Dummy's third heart winner will take care of 1 of these losers. Prospects of disposing of South's other loser are not good.\n\nAfter drawing trump, South should cash the ♦A and cross to the dummy in clubs. Dummy's remaining heart should be cashed for a diamond discard. A low diamond should be played from dummy and ruffed in the closed hand.\n\nWhen the ♦K ruffs out, the ♦Q will take care of South's club loser. Dummy still has a club entry to get to the ♦Q.\n\nIf the ♦K does not ruff out, South has one more chance. If West has the ♦K and 4 or more clubs, he can be squeezed. South should run his trumps.\n\nWest will have to give up a trick on the lead of the last spade.",
